  "supersedes": "RBM-001 v2.1.0",
  "amendment_rationale": "v2.1.0 let agents hold reviewer seats but kept ratification human, and ratification requires two separated humans. An organisation with one human could therefore conduct a complete review and never sign the result, leaving governed decisions permanently unratified. v2.2.0 permits a single named human to ratify while the profile is non-binding, recording the decision as single-authority so it is never mistaken for a two-signature decision. It cannot be used once the profile is ACTIVE.",
